module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.ExteriorPower
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Monoidal
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Functoriality
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicTopology.SimplicialObject.Homotopy.Cosimplicial

/-!
# Cosimplicial modules and homotopy

Let `A` be a cosimplicial commutative ring, i.e. a functor from the simplex category to
commutative rings.  A cosimplicial module over `A` is a family of `A_n`-modules together with
transition maps which are semilinear over the transition maps of `A`.  Two homomorphisms of
cosimplicial modules are homotopic when they are connected by the equivalence relation
generated by the cosimplicial homotopies of [Stacks, Tag 07KB].

This file records the four stability properties of that relation asserted by clauses (1)-(4)
of Stacks Lemma 07KQ: homotopy is preserved by tensoring with a fixed cosimplicial module, by
passing to a fixed exterior power, by base change along a homomorphism of cosimplicial rings,
and by completion along a cosimplicial ideal.

Two presentations of a cosimplicial module occur, and the file keeps both.  Tensor products,
exterior powers and base change are degreewise constructions on modules over a varying ring,
which is exactly the datum of a presheaf of modules over the presheaf of rings attached to `A`;
`CosimplicialModule` is that presentation, and it inherits the monoidal and exterior-power API
of `PresheafOfModules`.  Completion, on the other hand, must let the module carriers live in a
universe independent of the universe of the rings, so for that result the data are bundled by
hand as `SemilinearCosimplicialModule`.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.CosimplicialModule` — a cosimplicial module over a cosimplicial ring, as a
  presheaf of modules over the presheaf of rings `Crystalline.cosimplicialRingPresheaf`.
* `Crystalline.Homotopy` — a homotopy between two homomorphisms of cosimplicial modules, given
  degreewise by linear maps indexed by the simplices of `Δ[1]`.
* `Crystalline.Homotopic` — the equivalence relation generated by homotopies.
* `Crystalline.ExteriorPowerFunctor` — the degreewise exterior power of a cosimplicial module,
  specified by its values on exterior products.
* `Crystalline.baseChangeObj` — the base change `S ⊗_R M` of a module along a ring
  homomorphism `φ : R →+* S`, together with `Crystalline.semilinearBaseChangeMap`, the base
  change of a semilinear map.
* `Crystalline.baseChange` — the base change functor on cosimplicial modules along a
  homomorphism of cosimplicial rings, degreewise `K_n ↦ B_n ⊗_{A_n} K_n`.
* `Crystalline.SemilinearCosimplicialModule` — a cosimplicial module presented by its
  degreewise modules and semilinear transition maps, with carriers in an independent universe.
* `Crystalline.CosimplicialIdeal` — an ideal in each degree of `A`, carried into the next by
  every transition map.
* `Crystalline.SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion` — a realization of the degreewise adic
  completion of such a module, together with the continuous semilinear cosimplicial structure
  that characterizes it.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.homotopic_tensor_id` — tensoring on the right preserves homotopic morphisms.
* `Crystalline.homotopic_exteriorPower_map` — exterior powers preserve homotopic morphisms.
* `Crystalline.homotopic_baseChange` — base change along a homomorphism of cosimplicial rings
  preserves homotopic morphisms.
* `Crystalline.homotopic_adicCompletionMap` — the maps induced on completions by homotopic maps
  are homotopic.

## Implementation notes

`PresheafOfModules` is used with the indexing category opposite to the simplex category; the
canonical equivalence from the double opposite then makes its objects precisely the families of
modules over the rings `A_n`.  `Homotopy` is the degreewise description of
`CategoryTheory.CosimplicialObject.Homotopy`, with linear components and the restriction of
scalars that the varying rings require.

The generator equations of `ExteriorPowerFunctor` require both the cosimplicial transition maps
and the maps on homomorphisms to be the canonical exterior-power maps; objectwise isomorphisms
alone would not express this.

`PresheafOfModules` carries only restriction of scalars along a morphism of presheaves of
rings, so base change is built here by hand: `baseChangeObj` is the degreewise tensor product
and `semilinearBaseChangeMap` is the general map `S ⊗_R M → S' ⊗_{R'} M'` induced by a square
of ring maps and a semilinear map, which supplies both the cosimplicial transition maps of
`baseChangePresheaf` (where the rings vary) and the action of `baseChange` on homomorphisms
and on homotopy components (where they do not).  The tensor factors are written in the order
`B_n ⊗_{A_n} K_n`, which is the order Mathlib's module structures support; Stacks writes
`K_n ⊗_{A_n} B_n`, canonically isomorphic over the commutative ring `A_n`.  The components of
a `Homotopy` between cosimplicial `B`-modules are morphisms of `B_n`-modules, which is the
`B_*`-linearity that clause (3) of 07KQ demands of the base-changed homotopy.

A `Completion` records objectwise linear equivalences with Mathlib's `AdicCompletion`.  Its
scalar and module transition maps are semilinear, adically continuous, and agree with the
original maps on the canonical dense images; these conditions characterize the canonical
extensions, rather than allowing arbitrary additive extensions.  The completed homomorphisms in
`homotopic_adicCompletionMap` are pinned objectwise to `AdicCompletion.map`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07KQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07KQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Crystalline

section PresheafPresentation

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory Opposite Simplicial

universe u

/-- The presheaf of rings associated to a cosimplicial ring, indexed using the double
opposite of the simplex category as required by `PresheafOfModules`. -/
public abbrev cosimplicialRingPresheaf (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) :=
  unopUnop SimplexCategory ⋙ A ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat

/-- A cosimplicial module over a cosimplicial commutative ring `A`. -/
public abbrev CosimplicialModule (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) :=
  PresheafOfModules.{u}
    ((unopUnop SimplexCategory ⋙ A) ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat)

/-- The rings of the presheaf underlying `CosimplicialModule A` are commutative; instance
search does not see through the composite functor, so the instance is given by hand. -/
public instance commRingCosimplicialModuleRingObj
    (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) (X : (SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ)ᵒᵖ) :
    CommRing (((unopUnop SimplexCategory ⋙ A) ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj X) :=
  inferInstanceAs (CommRing (A.obj (unop (unop X))))

variable {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}
  {K M : CosimplicialModule A}

/-- A homotopy between two morphisms of cosimplicial modules.  Its components are
`A_n`-linear maps indexed by the `n`-simplices of `Δ[1]`; the displayed compatibility is
the degreewise homotopy equation. -/
public structure Homotopy (a b : K ⟶ M) where
  /-- The component of the homotopy in degree `n` at a simplex `α ∈ Δ[1]_n`. -/
  app (n : SimplexCategory) (α : (Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).obj (op n)) :
    K.obj (op (op n)) ⟶ M.obj (op (op n))
  /-- Compatibility of the components with the cosimplicial structure maps. -/
  naturality {n m : SimplexCategory} (f : n ⟶ m)
      (α : (Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).obj (op m)) :
    K.map f.op.op ≫
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalars ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).map f.op.op).hom).map
          (app m α) =
      app n ((Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).map f.op α) ≫ M.map f.op.op
  /-- The endpoint at the constant zero simplex is `a`. -/
  app_zero (n : SimplexCategory) :
    app n (SSet.stdSimplex.const 1 0 (op n)) = a.app (op (op n))
  /-- The endpoint at the constant one simplex is `b`. -/
  app_one (n : SimplexCategory) :
    app n (SSet.stdSimplex.const 1 1 (op n)) = b.app (op (op n))

/-- Two morphisms of cosimplicial modules are homotopic if they are related by the
equivalence relation generated by directed homotopies. -/
public abbrev Homotopic (a b : K ⟶ M) : Prop :=
  Relation.EqvGen (fun a b ↦ Nonempty (Homotopy a b)) a b

/-- **Stacks Lemma 07KQ (tensor).** Tensoring homotopic morphisms of cosimplicial modules
with the identity morphism of another cosimplicial module preserves homotopy. -/
@[stacks 07KQ "tensor"]
public theorem homotopic_tensor_id {φ ψ : K ⟶ M} (h : Homotopic φ ψ)
    (L : CosimplicialModule A) :
    Homotopic (φ ⊗ₘ 𝟙 L) (ψ ⊗ₘ 𝟙 L) := by
  apply Relation.EqvGen.map (fun f => f ⊗ₘ 𝟙 L) (fun a b h => ?_) h
  obtain ⟨h⟩ := h
  refine ⟨{ app := fun n α => h.app n α ⊗ₘ 𝟙 (L.obj (op (op n))),
            naturality := ?_, app_zero := ?_, app_one := ?_ }⟩
  · intro n m f α; apply ModuleCat.MonoidalCategory.tensor_ext; intro k l
    change h.app m α (K.map f.op.op k) ⊗ₜ L.map f.op.op l =
      M.map f.op.op (h.app n ((Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).map f.op α) k) ⊗ₜ L.map f.op.op l
    congr 1; exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (h.naturality f α) k
  · intro n; rw [h.app_zero]; rfl
  · intro n; rw [h.app_one]; rfl

end PresheafPresentation

section ExteriorPower

open CategoryTheory Opposite Simplicial

universe u

/-- The rings of the presheaf attached to a cosimplicial commutative ring are commutative.
The forgetful functor to `RingCat` hides this, so the instance is restored by hand. -/
public instance commRingCosimplicialRingPresheafObj
    (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) (X : (SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ)ᵒᵖ) :
    CommRing ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj X) :=
  inferInstanceAs (CommRing (A.obj (unop (unop X))))

/-- The exterior power of a semilinear map of modules: for a ring homomorphism `φ : R →+* S`
and an `R`-linear map `f : M → N` to the restriction of scalars of an `S`-module `N`, the map
sending `x₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ x_i` to `f x₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ f x_i`. -/
public noncomputable def semilinearExteriorPowerMap {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (φ : R →+* S) {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {N : ModuleCat.{u} S}
    (f : M ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).obj N) (i : ℕ) :
    M.exteriorPower i ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).obj (N.exteriorPower i) := by
  let alt : M.AlternatingMap ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).obj (N.exteriorPower i)) i :=
    { toFun := fun x => ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk (R := S) (M := N) (fun j => f (x j))
      map_update_add' := fun m j x y => by
        have hfun : (fun k => f (Function.update m j (x + y) k)) =
            Function.update (fun k => f (m k)) j (f x + f y) := by
          funext k
          by_cases hk : k = j <;> simp [Function.update, hk, map_add]
        have hx : (fun k => f (Function.update m j x k)) =
            Function.update (fun k => f (m k)) j (f x) := by
          funext k
          by_cases hk : k = j <;> simp [Function.update, hk]
        have hy : (fun k => f (Function.update m j y k)) =
            Function.update (fun k => f (m k)) j (f y) := by
          funext k
          by_cases hk : k = j <;> simp [Function.update, hk]
        rw [hfun, hx, hy]
        exact ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk.map_update_add (R := S) (M := N)
          (fun k => f (m k)) j (f x) (f y)
      map_update_smul' := fun m j c x => by
        have hfun : (fun k => f (Function.update m j (c • x) k)) =
            Function.update (fun k => f (m k)) j (φ c • f x) := by
          funext k
          by_cases hk : k = j
          · subst hk
            simp only [Function.update_self]
            exact (f.hom.map_smul c x).trans
              (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.smul_def φ c (f x))
          · simp only [Function.update_of_ne hk]
        have hx : (fun k => f (Function.update m j x k)) =
            Function.update (fun k => f (m k)) j (f x) := by
          funext k
          by_cases hk : k = j <;> simp [Function.update, hk]
        rw [hfun, hx]
        change ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk (R := S) (M := N)
            (Function.update (fun k => f (m k)) j (φ c • f x)) =
          c • (show (ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).obj (N.exteriorPower i) from
            ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk (R := S) (M := N)
              (Function.update (fun k => f (m k)) j (f x)))
        rw [ModuleCat.restrictScalars.smul_def]
        exact ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk.map_update_smul (R := S) (M := N)
          (fun k => f (m k)) j (φ c) (f x)
      map_eq_zero_of_eq' := fun m a b hab habne => by
        change ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk (R := S) (M := N)
          (fun k => (f (m k) : N)) = 0
        exact ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk.map_eq_zero_of_eq (R := S) (M := N)
          (fun k => (f (m k) : N)) (congrArg f hab) habne }
  exact ModuleCat.exteriorPower.desc alt

/-- The exterior power of a semilinear map takes an exterior product of elements to the
exterior product of their images. -/
public theorem semilinearExteriorPowerMap_mk {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (φ : R →+* S) {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {N : ModuleCat.{u} S}
    (f : M ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).obj N) (i : ℕ) (x : Fin i → M) :
    semilinearExteriorPowerMap φ f i (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x) =
      ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk (R := S) (M := N) (fun j => (f (x j) : N)) := by
  classical
  unfold semilinearExteriorPowerMap
  exact ModuleCat.exteriorPower.desc_mk _ x

/-- A functorial degreewise exterior power on modules over a cosimplicial ring. -/
public structure ExteriorPowerFunctor (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u})
    (i : ℕ) where
  /-- The exterior-power functor on cosimplicial modules. -/
  functor : CosimplicialModule A ⥤ CosimplicialModule A
  /-- Identification with the usual exterior power in each degree. -/
  componentIso (K : CosimplicialModule A) (n : SimplexCategory) :
    (functor.obj K).obj (op (op n)) ≅ (K.obj (op (op n))).exteriorPower i
  /-- The transition maps act on exterior products by applying the original
  semilinear transition map to each factor. -/
  transition_mk (K : CosimplicialModule A) {n m : SimplexCategory}
      (f : n ⟶ m) (x : Fin i → K.obj (op (op n))) :
    (componentIso K m).hom
        ((functor.obj K).map f.op.op
          ((componentIso K n).inv (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x))) =
      ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk
        (fun j ↦ (show K.obj (op (op m)) from K.map f.op.op (x j)))
  /-- The map on homomorphisms is the usual exterior-power map in each degree. -/
  map_mk {K M : CosimplicialModule A} (φ : K ⟶ M)
      (n : SimplexCategory) (x : Fin i → K.obj (op (op n))) :
    (componentIso M n).hom
        (((functor.map φ).app (op (op n)))
          ((componentIso K n).inv (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x))) =
      ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk
        (fun j ↦ φ.app (op (op n)) (x j))

/-- The canonical degreewise exterior-power construction for a cosimplicial module
over a varying cosimplicial ring. -/
public noncomputable def exteriorPowerFunctor
    (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) (i : ℕ) :
    ExteriorPowerFunctor A i where
  functor :=
    { obj := fun K =>
        { obj := fun X => (K.obj X).exteriorPower i
          map := fun {X Y} f =>
            semilinearExteriorPowerMap
              ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).map f).hom (K.map f) i
          map_id := by
            intro X
            apply ModuleCat.exteriorPower.hom_ext
            apply AlternatingMap.ext
            intro x
            change semilinearExteriorPowerMap
                (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map (𝟙 (unop (unop X))))) (K.map (𝟙 X)) i
                (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x) =
              (ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'App
                (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map (𝟙 (unop (unop X)))))
                (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map_id (unop (unop X))))
                ((K.obj X).exteriorPower i)).inv (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x)
            simp only [PresheafOfModules.map_id, Functor.comp_obj, unopUnop_obj,
              CommRingCat.forgetToRingCat_obj, Functor.comp_map, unopUnop_map, unop_id,
              CommRingCat.forgetToRingCat_map_hom, ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'_inv_app,
              ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'App_inv_apply, semilinearExteriorPowerMap_mk]
            exact congrArg (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk
                (R := (cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj X) (M := K.obj X))
              (funext fun j ↦ ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'App_inv_apply
                (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map (𝟙 (unop (unop X)))))
                (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map_id (unop (unop X))))
                (K.obj X) (x j))
          map_comp := by
            intro X Y Z f g
            apply ModuleCat.exteriorPower.hom_ext
            apply AlternatingMap.ext
            intro x
            change semilinearExteriorPowerMap
                (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map (f.unop.unop ≫ g.unop.unop)))
                (K.map (f ≫ g)) i (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x) =
              (ModuleCat.restrictScalarsComp'App
                (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map f.unop.unop))
                (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map g.unop.unop))
                (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map (f.unop.unop ≫ g.unop.unop)))
                (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map_comp f.unop.unop g.unop.unop))
                ((K.obj Z).exteriorPower i)).inv
                (semilinearExteriorPowerMap
                  (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map g.unop.unop)) (K.map g) i
                  (semilinearExteriorPowerMap
                    (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map f.unop.unop)) (K.map f) i
                    (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x)))
            rw [semilinearExteriorPowerMap_mk
                (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map f.unop.unop)) (K.map f) i x,
              semilinearExteriorPowerMap_mk
                (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (A.map g.unop.unop)) (K.map g) i
                (fun j ↦ (show K.obj Y from K.map f (x j)))]
            exact Eq.trans (semilinearExteriorPowerMap_mk _ (K.map (f ≫ g)) i x)
              (congrArg (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk
                  (R := (cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj Z) (M := K.obj Z))
                (funext fun j ↦ PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply K f g (x j))) }
      map := fun {K M} φ =>
        { app := fun X => ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (φ.app X) i
          naturality := by
            intro X Y f
            apply ModuleCat.exteriorPower.hom_ext
            apply AlternatingMap.ext
            intro x
            change (ModuleCat.restrictScalars
                (RingCat.Hom.hom (((unopUnop SimplexCategory ⋙ A) ⋙
                  forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).map f))).map
                (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (φ.app Y) i)
                (semilinearExteriorPowerMap
                  (RingCat.Hom.hom ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).map f))
                  (K.map f) i (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x)) =
              semilinearExteriorPowerMap
                (RingCat.Hom.hom ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).map f))
                (M.map f) i (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (φ.app X) i
                  (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x))
            simp only [semilinearExteriorPowerMap_mk, ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map_mk]
            change ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (φ.app Y) i
                (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk
                  (R := (cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj Y) (M := K.obj Y)
                  (fun j ↦ (show K.obj Y from K.map f (x j)))) =
              ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk
                (R := (cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj Y) (M := M.obj Y)
                (fun j ↦ M.map f (φ.app X (x j)))
            rw [ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map_mk]
            exact congrArg (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk
                (R := (cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj Y) (M := M.obj Y))
              (funext fun j ↦ PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply φ f (x j)) }
      map_id := by
        intro K
        apply PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
        intro X
        apply ModuleCat.exteriorPower.hom_ext
        apply AlternatingMap.ext
        intro x
        change ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (𝟙 (K.obj X)) i
            (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x) = ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x
        rw [ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map_mk]
        rfl
      map_comp := by
        intro K M N φ ψ
        apply PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
        intro X
        apply ModuleCat.exteriorPower.hom_ext
        apply AlternatingMap.ext
        intro x
        change ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (φ.app X ≫ ψ.app X) i
            (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x) =
          (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (φ.app X) i ≫
            ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (ψ.app X) i) (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x)
        simp only [ModuleCat.comp_apply, ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map_mk]
        apply congrArg (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk
          (R := (cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj X) (M := N.obj X))
        funext j
        rfl }
  componentIso := fun K n => Iso.refl _
  transition_mk := by
    intro K n m f x
    simp [semilinearExteriorPowerMap_mk]
  map_mk := by
    intro K M φ n x
    simp [ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map_mk]
    rfl

/-- **Stacks 07KQ, exterior power.** Homotopic homomorphisms of cosimplicial
modules induce homotopic homomorphisms on every exterior power. -/
@[stacks 07KQ "exterior_power"]
public theorem homotopic_exteriorPower_map
    {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}
    {K M : CosimplicialModule A} {φ ψ : K ⟶ M} (i : ℕ)
    (h : Homotopic φ ψ) :
    Homotopic ((exteriorPowerFunctor A i).functor.map φ)
      ((exteriorPowerFunctor A i).functor.map ψ) := by
  let F := exteriorPowerFunctor A i
  have liftHomotopy {f g : K ⟶ M} (hh : Homotopy f g) :
      Homotopy (F.functor.map f) (F.functor.map g) := by
    refine
      { app := fun n α => ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (hh.app n α) i
        naturality := by
          intro n m q α
          apply ModuleCat.exteriorPower.hom_ext
          apply AlternatingMap.ext
          intro x
          change (ModuleCat.restrictScalars
              (RingCat.Hom.hom ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).map q.op.op))).map
              (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (hh.app m α) i)
              (semilinearExteriorPowerMap
                (RingCat.Hom.hom ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).map q.op.op))
                (K.map q.op.op) i (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x)) =
            semilinearExteriorPowerMap
              (RingCat.Hom.hom ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).map q.op.op))
              (M.map q.op.op) i
              (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map
                (hh.app n ((Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).map q.op α)) i
                (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x))
          simp only [semilinearExteriorPowerMap_mk, ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map_mk]
          exact Eq.trans
            (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map_mk (hh.app m α)
              (fun j ↦ (show K.obj (op (op m)) from K.map q.op.op (x j))))
            (congrArg (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk
                (R := (cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj (op (op m)))
                (M := M.obj (op (op m))))
              (funext fun j ↦ CategoryTheory.congr_fun (hh.naturality q α) (x j)))
        app_zero := by
          intro n
          exact congrArg (fun t => ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map t i) (hh.app_zero n)
        app_one := by
          intro n
          exact congrArg (fun t => ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map t i) (hh.app_one n) }
  exact Relation.EqvGen.map (fun f => F.functor.map f) (fun _ _ ⟨hab⟩ => ⟨liftHomotopy hab⟩) h

end ExteriorPower

section BaseChange

open CategoryTheory Opposite Simplicial TensorProduct

universe u

/-! #### Base change of a single module along a ring homomorphism -/

/-- The base change of an `R`-module `M` along a ring homomorphism `φ : R →+* S`: the
`S`-module `S ⊗_R M`, where `S` is regarded as an `R`-module through `φ`. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeObj {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (φ : R →+* S)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) : ModuleCat.{u} S :=
  letI := φ.toAlgebra
  ModuleCat.of S (TensorProduct R S M)

/-- The generator `s ⊗ m` of the base change `S ⊗_R M`. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeMk {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (φ : R →+* S)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (s : S) (m : M) : baseChangeObj φ M :=
  letI := φ.toAlgebra
  s ⊗ₜ[R] m

section

variable {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]

/-- The generators `s ⊗ m` exhaust the base change: a property of elements of `S ⊗_R M`
which holds at zero and at every generator and is stable under addition holds everywhere. -/
public theorem baseChangeObj_induction (φ : R →+* S) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    {motive : baseChangeObj φ M → Prop} (zero : motive 0)
    (mk : ∀ (s : S) (m : M), motive (baseChangeMk φ M s m))
    (add : ∀ x y, motive x → motive y → motive (x + y)) (z : baseChangeObj φ M) : motive z :=
  let _ := φ.toAlgebra
  TensorProduct.induction_on z zero mk add

/-- The generator `s ⊗ 0` of the base change is zero. -/
@[simp]
public theorem baseChangeMk_zero_right (φ : R →+* S) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (s : S) :
    baseChangeMk φ M s 0 = 0 := by
  let _ := φ.toAlgebra
  change (s ⊗ₜ[R] (0 : M) : TensorProduct R S M) = 0
  rw [TensorProduct.tmul_zero]

/-- The generator `s ⊗ m` is additive in the module factor. -/
@[simp]
public theorem baseChangeMk_add_right (φ : R →+* S) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (s : S) (m m' : M) :
    baseChangeMk φ M s (m + m') = baseChangeMk φ M s m + baseChangeMk φ M s m' := by
  let _ := φ.toAlgebra
  change (s ⊗ₜ[R] (m + m') : TensorProduct R S M) = s ⊗ₜ[R] m + s ⊗ₜ[R] m'
  rw [TensorProduct.tmul_add]

/-- The generator `s ⊗ m` is additive in the ring factor. -/
@[simp]
public theorem baseChangeMk_add_left (φ : R →+* S) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (s s' : S) (m : M) :
    baseChangeMk φ M (s + s') m = baseChangeMk φ M s m + baseChangeMk φ M s' m := by
  let _ := φ.toAlgebra
  change ((s + s') ⊗ₜ[R] m : TensorProduct R S M) = s ⊗ₜ[R] m + s' ⊗ₜ[R] m
  rw [TensorProduct.add_tmul]

/-- The base change is an `S`-module through the ring factor: `s • (s' ⊗ m) = (s * s') ⊗ m`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem smul_baseChangeMk (φ : R →+* S) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (s s' : S) (m : M) :
    s • baseChangeMk φ M s' m = baseChangeMk φ M (s * s') m := by
  let _ := φ.toAlgebra
  change (s • (s' ⊗ₜ[R] m) : TensorProduct R S M) = (s * s') ⊗ₜ[R] m
  rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul]

/-- A scalar from the base ring may be moved across the tensor sign. -/
public theorem baseChangeMk_smul (φ : R →+* S) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (r : R) (s : S) (m : M) :
    baseChangeMk φ M (φ r * s) m = baseChangeMk φ M s (r • m) := by
  let _ := φ.toAlgebra
  change ((φ r * s) ⊗ₜ[R] m : TensorProduct R S M) = s ⊗ₜ[R] (r • m)
  rw [show φ r * s = r • s from rfl, TensorProduct.smul_tmul]

/-- Two morphisms out of a base change agree as soon as they agree on the generators. -/
public theorem baseChange_hom_ext {φ : R →+* S} {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {N : ModuleCat.{u} S}
    {g h : baseChangeObj φ M ⟶ N}
    (H : ∀ (s : S) (m : M), g (baseChangeMk φ M s m) = h (baseChangeMk φ M s m)) : g = h := by
  refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun z => ?_)
  induction z using baseChangeObj_induction with
  | zero => rw [map_zero, map_zero]
  | mk s m => exact H s m
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy]

/-- A `σ`-semilinear map between the carriers of two modules, read as a morphism into the
restriction of scalars along `σ`. -/
public noncomputable def ofSemilinearMap (σ : R →+* S) {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {N : ModuleCat.{u} S}
    (g : M →ₛₗ[σ] N) : M ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars σ).obj N :=
  ModuleCat.ofHom (X := M) (Y := (ModuleCat.restrictScalars σ).obj N)
    { toFun := g
      map_add' := map_add g
      map_smul' := fun r x => map_smulₛₗ g r x }

/-- `ofSemilinearMap σ g` acts on elements as `g`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem ofSemilinearMap_apply (σ : R →+* S) {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {N : ModuleCat.{u} S}
    (g : M →ₛₗ[σ] N) (x : M) : ofSemilinearMap σ g x = g x := rfl

/-- The `σ`-semilinear map underlying a morphism into the restriction of scalars along `σ`. -/
public noncomputable def toSemilinearMap (σ : R →+* S) {M : ModuleCat.{u} R}
    {N : ModuleCat.{u} S} (g : M ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars σ).obj N) : M →ₛₗ[σ] N where
  toFun := g
  map_add' := map_add g.hom
  map_smul' r x := g.hom.map_smul r x

/-- `toSemilinearMap σ g` acts on elements as `g`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem toSemilinearMap_apply (σ : R →+* S) {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {N : ModuleCat.{u} S}
    (g : M ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars σ).obj N) (x : M) : toSemilinearMap σ g x = g x := rfl

end

section

variable {R S R' S' : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [CommRing R'] [CommRing S']

/-- The `R`-balanced biadditive datum underlying `semilinearBaseChangeMap`:
the assignment `(s, m) ↦ σ s ⊗ g m`, additive in each variable. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeBalanced (φ' : R' →+* S') {ρ : R →+* R'} (σ : S →+* S')
    {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {M' : ModuleCat.{u} R'} (g : M →ₛₗ[ρ] M') :
    S →+ (M →+ baseChangeObj φ' M') :=
  AddMonoidHom.mk'
    (fun s => AddMonoidHom.mk' (fun m => baseChangeMk φ' M' (σ s) (g m)) (by intro m m'; simp))
    (by intro s s'; ext m; simp)

/-- `baseChangeBalanced` sends `(s, m)` to the generator `σ s ⊗ g m`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem baseChangeBalanced_apply (φ' : R' →+* S') {ρ : R →+* R'} (σ : S →+* S')
    {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {M' : ModuleCat.{u} R'} (g : M →ₛₗ[ρ] M') (s : S) (m : M) :
    baseChangeBalanced φ' σ g s m = baseChangeMk φ' M' (σ s) (g m) := rfl

/-- `baseChangeBalanced` is balanced over the base ring: a scalar of `R` passes from the
ring factor to the module factor. -/
public theorem baseChangeBalanced_mul (φ : R →+* S) (φ' : R' →+* S') {ρ : R →+* R'}
    (σ : S →+* S') (hc : ∀ r, σ (φ r) = φ' (ρ r))
    {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {M' : ModuleCat.{u} R'} (g : M →ₛₗ[ρ] M') (r : R) (s : S) (m : M) :
    baseChangeBalanced φ' σ g (φ r * s) m = baseChangeBalanced φ' σ g s (r • m) := by
  change baseChangeMk φ' M' (σ (φ r * s)) (g m) = baseChangeMk φ' M' (σ s) (g (r • m))
  rw [map_mul, hc, baseChangeMk_smul, map_smulₛₗ]

/-- The additive map underlying `semilinearBaseChangeMap`. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeAddHom (φ : R →+* S) (φ' : R' →+* S') {ρ : R →+* R'}
    (σ : S →+* S') (hc : ∀ r, σ (φ r) = φ' (ρ r))
    {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {M' : ModuleCat.{u} R'} (g : M →ₛₗ[ρ] M') :
    baseChangeObj φ M →+ baseChangeObj φ' M' :=
  letI := φ.toAlgebra
  TensorProduct.liftAddHom (baseChangeBalanced φ' σ g) (baseChangeBalanced_mul φ φ' σ hc g)

/-- `baseChangeAddHom` sends the generator `s ⊗ m` to `σ s ⊗ g m`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem baseChangeAddHom_mk (φ : R →+* S) (φ' : R' →+* S') {ρ : R →+* R'}
    (σ : S →+* S') (hc : ∀ r, σ (φ r) = φ' (ρ r))
    {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {M' : ModuleCat.{u} R'} (g : M →ₛₗ[ρ] M') (s : S) (m : M) :
    baseChangeAddHom φ φ' σ hc g (baseChangeMk φ M s m) = baseChangeMk φ' M' (σ s) (g m) := rfl

/-- The base change of a semilinear map.  Given ring homomorphisms `φ : R →+* S`,
`φ' : R' →+* S'`, `ρ : R →+* R'` and `σ : S →+* S'` with `σ ∘ φ = φ' ∘ ρ`, and a
`ρ`-semilinear map `g : M → M'`, this is the `σ`-semilinear map `S ⊗_R M → S' ⊗_{R'} M'`
determined by `s ⊗ m ↦ σ s ⊗ g m`. -/
public noncomputable def semilinearBaseChangeMap (φ : R →+* S) (φ' : R' →+* S') {ρ : R →+* R'}
    (σ : S →+* S') (hc : ∀ r, σ (φ r) = φ' (ρ r))
    {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {M' : ModuleCat.{u} R'} (g : M →ₛₗ[ρ] M') :
    baseChangeObj φ M →ₛₗ[σ] baseChangeObj φ' M' where
  toFun := baseChangeAddHom φ φ' σ hc g
  map_add' := map_add _
  map_smul' s z := by
    induction z using baseChangeObj_induction with
    | zero => rw [smul_zero, map_zero, smul_zero]
    | mk s' m =>
        rw [smul_baseChangeMk, baseChangeAddHom_mk, baseChangeAddHom_mk, map_mul,
          smul_baseChangeMk]
    | add x y hx hy => rw [smul_add, map_add, map_add, hx, hy, smul_add]

/-- `semilinearBaseChangeMap` sends the generator `s ⊗ m` to `σ s ⊗ g m`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem semilinearBaseChangeMap_mk (φ : R →+* S) (φ' : R' →+* S') {ρ : R →+* R'}
    (σ : S →+* S') (hc : ∀ r, σ (φ r) = φ' (ρ r))
    {M : ModuleCat.{u} R} {M' : ModuleCat.{u} R'} (g : M →ₛₗ[ρ] M') (s : S) (m : M) :
    semilinearBaseChangeMap φ φ' σ hc g (baseChangeMk φ M s m) =
      baseChangeMk φ' M' (σ s) (g m) := rfl

end

section

variable {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]

/-- The base change of an `R`-linear map along `φ : R →+* S`. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeMap (φ : R →+* S) {M N : ModuleCat.{u} R} (g : M ⟶ N) :
    baseChangeObj φ M ⟶ baseChangeObj φ N :=
  ModuleCat.ofHom (semilinearBaseChangeMap φ φ (RingHom.id S) (fun _ => rfl) g.hom)

/-- `baseChangeMap φ g` sends the generator `s ⊗ m` to `s ⊗ g m`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem baseChangeMap_mk (φ : R →+* S) {M N : ModuleCat.{u} R} (g : M ⟶ N) (s : S)
    (m : M) : baseChangeMap φ g (baseChangeMk φ M s m) = baseChangeMk φ N s (g m) := rfl

end

/-! #### Base change of cosimplicial modules -/

variable {A B : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}

/-- A homomorphism of cosimplicial rings, read as a morphism of the attached presheaves
of rings. -/
public def cosimplicialRingPresheafMap (f : A ⟶ B) :
    cosimplicialRingPresheaf A ⟶ cosimplicialRingPresheaf B :=
  Functor.whiskerLeft (unopUnop SimplexCategory)
    (Functor.whiskerRight f (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat))

/-- The ring homomorphism `A_X → B_X` in degree `X` underlying a homomorphism of
cosimplicial rings. -/
public abbrev baseRingHom (f : A ⟶ B) (X : (SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ)ᵒᵖ) :
    (cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj X →+* (cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).obj X :=
  ((cosimplicialRingPresheafMap f).app X).hom

/-- The degreewise ring homomorphisms of a homomorphism of cosimplicial rings commute with the
cosimplicial structure maps. -/
public theorem baseRingHom_naturality (f : A ⟶ B) {X Y : (SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ)ᵒᵖ} (π : X ⟶ Y)
    (r : (cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).obj X) :
    ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map π).hom (baseRingHom f X r) =
      baseRingHom f Y (((cosimplicialRingPresheaf A).map π).hom r) := by
  have eq := RingHom.congr_fun
    (congrArg RingCat.Hom.hom ((cosimplicialRingPresheafMap f).naturality π)) r
  dsimp at eq
  exact eq.symm

/-- The base change of a cosimplicial module along a homomorphism of cosimplicial rings
`f : A ⟶ B`.  In degree `n` it is the `B_n`-module `B_n ⊗_{A_n} K_n`, and the cosimplicial
structure maps send `s ⊗ x` to `B(π) s ⊗ K(π) x`. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangePresheaf (f : A ⟶ B) (K : CosimplicialModule A) :
    CosimplicialModule B where
  obj X := baseChangeObj (baseRingHom f X) (K.obj X)
  map {X Y} π := ofSemilinearMap ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map π).hom
    (semilinearBaseChangeMap (baseRingHom f X) (baseRingHom f Y)
      ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map π).hom (baseRingHom_naturality f π)
      (toSemilinearMap _ (K.map π)))
  map_id X := by
    refine baseChange_hom_ext fun s m => ?_
    have hs : ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map (𝟙 X)).hom s = s :=
      congrArg (fun t => (RingCat.Hom.hom t) s) ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map_id X)
    have hm : K.map (𝟙 X) m = m := by
      rw [K.map_id, ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'_inv_app]
      exact ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'App_inv_apply _ _ (K.obj X) m
    simp only [ofSemilinearMap_apply, semilinearBaseChangeMap_mk, toSemilinearMap_apply,
      ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'_inv_app, ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'App_inv_apply, hs, hm]
    exact rfl
  map_comp {X Y Z} π ϖ := by
    refine baseChange_hom_ext fun s m => ?_
    have hs : ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map (π ≫ ϖ)).hom s =
        ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map ϖ).hom (((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map π).hom s) :=
      RingHom.congr_fun
        (congrArg RingCat.Hom.hom ((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map_comp π ϖ)) s
    have hm : K.map (π ≫ ϖ) m = K.map ϖ (K.map π m) :=
      PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply K π ϖ m
    simp only [ofSemilinearMap_apply, semilinearBaseChangeMap_mk, toSemilinearMap_apply,
      CategoryTheory.comp_apply, ModuleCat.restrictScalarsComp'_inv_app, hs, hm]
    exact rfl

/-- The base change functor on cosimplicial modules along a homomorphism of cosimplicial
rings. -/
public noncomputable def baseChange (f : A ⟶ B) :
    CosimplicialModule A ⥤ CosimplicialModule B where
  obj K := baseChangePresheaf f K
  map {K M} ψ :=
    { app X := baseChangeMap (baseRingHom f X) (ψ.app X)
      naturality {X Y} π := by
        refine baseChange_hom_ext fun s m => ?_
        exact congrArg (baseChangeMk (baseRingHom f Y) (M.obj Y)
          (((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map π).hom s))
            (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply ψ π m) }
  map_id K :=
    PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun X => baseChange_hom_ext fun _ _ => rfl
  map_comp {K M N} ψ χ :=
    PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun X => baseChange_hom_ext fun _ _ => rfl

/-- The base change of a homotopy of cosimplicial modules: the homotopy `h ⊗ 1`, given in
degree `n` at a simplex `α` by `h_{n, α} ⊗ 1_{B_n}`. -/
public noncomputable def Homotopy.baseChange (f : A ⟶ B) {K M : CosimplicialModule A}
    {a b : K ⟶ M} (h : Homotopy a b) :
    Homotopy ((Crystalline.baseChange f).map a) ((Crystalline.baseChange f).map b) where
  app n α := baseChangeMap (baseRingHom f (op (op n))) (h.app n α)
  naturality {n m} π α := by
    refine baseChange_hom_ext fun s x => ?_
    exact congrArg (baseChangeMk (baseRingHom f (op (op m))) (M.obj (op (op m)))
      (((cosimplicialRingPresheaf B).map π.op.op).hom s))
        (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (h.naturality π α) x)
  app_zero n := by rw [h.app_zero]; rfl
  app_one n := by rw [h.app_one]; rfl

/-- **Stacks 07KQ, base change.** If two homomorphisms of cosimplicial `A`-modules are
homotopic and `f : A ⟶ B` is a homomorphism of cosimplicial rings, then the induced
homomorphisms of cosimplicial `B`-modules between the base changes are homotopic.  The
homotopy is `h ⊗ 1`, and in particular each of its components is `B_n`-linear, because
`Homotopy` for cosimplicial `B`-modules demands exactly that. -/
@[stacks 07KT "homotopy is preserved by base change along a homomorphism of cosimplicial rings",
  stacks 07KQ "base change"]
public theorem homotopic_baseChange (f : A ⟶ B) {K M : CosimplicialModule A} {φ ψ : K ⟶ M}
    (h : Homotopic φ ψ) :
    Homotopic ((baseChange f).map φ) ((baseChange f).map ψ) :=
  Relation.EqvGen.map (fun g => (baseChange f).map g) (fun _ _ ⟨hab⟩ => ⟨hab.baseChange f⟩) h

end BaseChange

section Completion

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Simplicial

universe u v u' v'

/-- A module over a cosimplicial commutative ring.  Its transition maps are semilinear along
the corresponding maps of the ring. -/
public structure SemilinearCosimplicialModule (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) where
  /-- The module in each cosimplicial degree. -/
  obj : SimplexCategory → Type v
  /-- The abelian group structure in each degree. -/
  addCommGroup (n) : AddCommGroup (obj n)
  /-- The `A_n`-module structure in degree `n`. -/
  module (n) : Module (A.obj n) (obj n)
  /-- The semilinear transition map. -/
  map {n m} (f : n ⟶ m) : obj n →ₛₗ[(A.map f).hom] obj m
  map_id_apply (n) (x : obj n) : map (𝟙 n) x = x
  map_comp_apply {n m l} (f : n ⟶ m) (g : m ⟶ l) (x : obj n) :
    map (f ≫ g) x = map g (map f x)

namespace SemilinearCosimplicialModule

/-- The abelian group structure on each degree of a module over a cosimplicial ring. -/
public instance (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) (M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A)
    (n : SimplexCategory) : AddCommGroup (M.obj n) := M.addCommGroup n

/-- Each degree `M_n` is a module over the ring `A_n`. -/
public instance (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) (M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A)
    (n : SimplexCategory) : Module (A.obj n) (M.obj n) := M.module n

/-- The underlying cosimplicial abelian group of a module over a cosimplicial ring. -/
public def toCosimplicialObject {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}
    (M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A) : CosimplicialObject AddCommGrpCat.{v} where
  obj n := AddCommGrpCat.of (M.obj n)
  map f := AddCommGrpCat.ofHom (M.map f).toAddHom
  map_id n := by ext x; exact M.map_id_apply n x
  map_comp f g := by ext x; exact M.map_comp_apply f g x

/-- A homomorphism of modules over a fixed cosimplicial ring. -/
public structure Hom {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}
    (K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A) where
  /-- The linear map in each degree. -/
  app (n) : K.obj n →ₗ[A.obj n] M.obj n
  naturality {n m} (f : n ⟶ m) (x : K.obj n) :
    M.map f (app n x) = app m (K.map f x)

/-- The morphism of underlying cosimplicial abelian groups. -/
public def Hom.toNatTrans {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A} (φ : Hom K M) :
    K.toCosimplicialObject ⟶ M.toCosimplicialObject where
  app n := AddCommGrpCat.ofHom (φ.app n).toAddHom
  naturality := by
    intro n m f
    ext x
    exact (φ.naturality f x).symm

/-- An `A`-linear homotopy between homomorphisms of cosimplicial `A`-modules. -/
public structure Homotopy {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A} (φ ψ : Hom K M) where
  /-- The homotopy of the underlying cosimplicial abelian groups. -/
  homotopy : CosimplicialObject.Homotopy φ.toNatTrans ψ.toNatTrans
  /-- Every component of the homotopy is linear in its cosimplicial degree. -/
  linear (n : SimplexCategory) (α : (Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).obj (op n))
      (r : A.obj n) (x : K.obj n) :
    (show M.obj n from (homotopy.h.app n ≫ Pi.π _ α) (r • x)) =
      r • (show M.obj n from (homotopy.h.app n ≫ Pi.π _ α) x)

end SemilinearCosimplicialModule

/-- A cosimplicial ideal is a degreewise ideal carried into the next ideal by every
cosimplicial structure map. -/
public structure CosimplicialIdeal (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) where
  /-- The ideal in each degree. -/
  obj (n) : Ideal (A.obj n)
  map_le {n m} (f : n ⟶ m) : Ideal.map (A.map f).hom (obj n) ≤ obj m

namespace SemilinearCosimplicialModule

/-- Algebraic continuity for a map between two adic completions: every target-adic
neighbourhood of zero contains the image of a source-adic neighbourhood of zero. -/
public def AdicContinuous {R : Type u} {S : Type u'} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (I : Ideal R) (J : Ideal S) {P : Type v} {Q : Type v'}
    [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P] [AddCommGroup Q] [Module S Q]
    (f : AdicCompletion I P → AdicCompletion J Q) : Prop :=
  ∀ n, ∃ m, ∀ x, AdicCompletion.eval I P m x = 0 →
    AdicCompletion.eval J Q n (f x) = 0

/-- A realization of the degreewise adic completion of a cosimplicial module.  Besides the
objectwise identifications, the remaining fields say that the cosimplicial maps are the
adic-continuous semilinear extensions of the original structure maps. -/
public structure Completion {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}
    (I : CosimplicialIdeal A) (M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A) where
  /-- The completed cosimplicial abelian group. -/
  obj : CosimplicialObject AddCommGrpCat.{v}
  /-- Each degree is a module over the adic completion of `A_n`. -/
  module (n) : Module (AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (A.obj n)) (obj.obj n)
  /-- Its identification with adic completion in every degree. -/
  iso (n) : obj.obj n ≃ₗ[AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (A.obj n)]
    AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (M.obj n)
  /-- The canonical map between the completed scalar rings along a cosimplicial map. -/
  ringMap {n m} (f : n ⟶ m) :
    AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (A.obj n) →+* AdicCompletion (I.obj m) (A.obj m)
  ringMap_id (n) : ringMap (𝟙 n) = RingHom.id _
  ringMap_comp {n m l} (f : n ⟶ m) (g : m ⟶ l) :
    ringMap (f ≫ g) = (ringMap g).comp (ringMap f)
  ringMap_of_naturality {n m} (f : n ⟶ m) (r : A.obj n) :
    ringMap f (AdicCompletion.of (I.obj n) (A.obj n) r) =
      AdicCompletion.of (I.obj m) (A.obj m) (A.map f r)
  /-- The maps of completed scalar rings are adic-continuous. -/
  ringMap_adicContinuous {n m} (f : n ⟶ m) :
    AdicContinuous (I.obj n) (I.obj m) (ringMap f)
  map_semilinear {n m} (f : n ⟶ m)
      (r : AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (A.obj n)) (x : obj.obj n) :
    obj.map f (r • x) = ringMap f r • obj.map f x
  of_naturality {n m} (f : n ⟶ m) (x : M.obj n) :
    iso m (obj.map f ((iso n).symm (AdicCompletion.of (I.obj n) (M.obj n) x))) =
      AdicCompletion.of (I.obj m) (M.obj m) (M.map f x)
  map_adicContinuous {n m} (f : n ⟶ m) :
    AdicContinuous (I.obj n) (I.obj m)
      (fun x => iso m (obj.map f ((iso n).symm x)))

/-- Each degree of a completion is a module over the adic completion of `A_n`. -/
public instance Completion.instModule {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}
    {I : CosimplicialIdeal A} {M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A} (Mhat : Completion I M)
    (n : SimplexCategory) : Module (AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (A.obj n)) (Mhat.obj.obj n) :=
  Mhat.module n

namespace Completion

/-- A homomorphism between two completed cosimplicial modules, linear in every degree. -/
public structure Hom {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}} {I : CosimplicialIdeal A}
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A} (Khat : Completion I K)
    (Mhat : Completion I M) where
  /-- The map of underlying cosimplicial abelian groups. -/
  hom : Khat.obj ⟶ Mhat.obj
  /-- Degreewise linearity over the completed ring. -/
  linear (n) (r : AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (A.obj n)) (x : Khat.obj.obj n) :
    hom.app n (r • x) = r • hom.app n x

/-- A degreewise linear homotopy between maps of completed cosimplicial modules. -/
public structure Homotopy {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}} {I : CosimplicialIdeal A}
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A} {Khat : Completion I K} {Mhat : Completion I M}
    (φ ψ : Hom Khat Mhat) where
  /-- The homotopy of underlying cosimplicial abelian groups. -/
  homotopy : CosimplicialObject.Homotopy φ.hom ψ.hom
  /-- Every component is linear over the completed ring in that degree. -/
  linear (n : SimplexCategory) (α : (Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).obj (op n))
      (r : AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (A.obj n)) (x : Khat.obj.obj n) :
    (homotopy.h.app n ≫ Pi.π _ α) (r • x) =
      r • (homotopy.h.app n ≫ Pi.π _ α) x

end Completion

end SemilinearCosimplicialModule

/-- Two additive maps between adic completions agree as soon as they are adically continuous
and agree on the canonical image of the uncompleted module, because every element of the
completion is approximated by that image to any prescribed order. -/
lemma adicContinuous_ext
    {R : Type u} {S : Type u'} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (I : Ideal R) (J : Ideal S)
    {P : Type v} {Q : Type v'} [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P] [AddCommGroup Q] [Module S Q]
    (f g : AdicCompletion I P →+ AdicCompletion J Q)
    (hf : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I J f)
    (hg : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I J g)
    (hof : ∀ x, f (AdicCompletion.of I P x) = g (AdicCompletion.of I P x)) : f = g := by
  refine AddMonoidHom.ext fun x => AdicCompletion.ext fun n => ?_
  obtain ⟨mf, hmf⟩ := hf n
  obtain ⟨mg, hmg⟩ := hg n
  let p := max mf mg
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective (I ^ p • (⊤ : Submodule R P))
    (AdicCompletion.eval I P p x)
  have hp : AdicCompletion.eval I P p (x - AdicCompletion.of I P y) = 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, AdicCompletion.eval_of, hy, sub_self]
  have hpf : AdicCompletion.eval I P mf (x - AdicCompletion.of I P y) = 0 := by
    simpa [p] using congrArg (AdicCompletion.transitionMap I P (Nat.le_max_left mf mg)) hp
  have hpg : AdicCompletion.eval I P mg (x - AdicCompletion.of I P y) = 0 := by
    simpa [p] using congrArg (AdicCompletion.transitionMap I P (Nat.le_max_right mf mg)) hp
  have hf0 := hmf (x - AdicCompletion.of I P y) hpf
  have hg0 := hmg (x - AdicCompletion.of I P y) hpg
  simp only [map_sub] at hf0 hg0
  change AdicCompletion.eval J Q n (f x) = AdicCompletion.eval J Q n (g x)
  exact (sub_eq_zero.mp hf0).trans <| (congrArg (AdicCompletion.eval J Q n) (hof y)).trans <|
    (sub_eq_zero.mp hg0).symm

/-- The map induced on adic completions by a linear map is adically continuous. -/
lemma adicContinuous_adicCompletionMap
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) {P : Type v} {Q : Type v'}
    [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P] [AddCommGroup Q] [Module R Q] (f : P →ₗ[R] Q) :
    SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I I (AdicCompletion.map I f) := by
  intro n
  refine ⟨n, fun x hx => ?_⟩
  change (AdicCompletion.map I f x).val n = 0
  rw [AdicCompletion.map_val_apply]
  change x.val n = 0 at hx
  rw [hx, map_zero]

/-- A composition of adically continuous maps is adically continuous. -/
lemma SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous.comp
    {R : Type u} {S : Type u'} {W : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [CommRing W]
    (I : Ideal R) (J : Ideal S) (L : Ideal W) {P : Type v} {Q : Type v'} {T : Type*}
    [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P] [AddCommGroup Q] [Module S Q]
    [AddCommGroup T] [Module W T]
    {f : AdicCompletion I P → AdicCompletion J Q}
    {g : AdicCompletion J Q → AdicCompletion L T}
    (hf : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I J f)
    (hg : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous J L g) :
    SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I L (g ∘ f) := by
  intro n
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hg n
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := hf m
  exact ⟨l, fun x hx => hm _ (hl x hx)⟩

/-- The map induced on completions in degree `n` by an `A_n`-linear map `K_n → M_n`, read
through the identifications of the completed modules with adic completions. -/
private noncomputable def completedComponent
    {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}} {I : CosimplicialIdeal A}
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A}
    (Khat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I K)
    (Mhat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I M)
    (n : SimplexCategory) (f : K.obj n →ₗ[A.obj n] M.obj n) :
    Khat.obj.obj n →+ Mhat.obj.obj n where
  toFun x := (Mhat.iso n).symm (AdicCompletion.map (I.obj n) f (Khat.iso n x))
  map_zero' := by simp
  map_add' x y := by simp

/-- Completing linear maps `K_n → M_n` and `K_m → M_m` that commute with the transition maps
along `f` yields completed maps that commute with the transition maps of the completions. -/
private theorem completedComponent_naturality
    {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}} {I : CosimplicialIdeal A}
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A}
    (Khat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I K)
    (Mhat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I M) {n m : SimplexCategory} (f : n ⟶ m)
    (g : K.obj m →ₗ[A.obj m] M.obj m) (g' : K.obj n →ₗ[A.obj n] M.obj n)
    (h : ∀ z, g (K.map f z) = M.map f (g' z)) (x : Khat.obj.obj n) :
    completedComponent Khat Mhat m g (Khat.obj.map f x) =
      Mhat.obj.map f (completedComponent Khat Mhat n g' x) := by
  apply (Mhat.iso m).injective
  let l : AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (K.obj n) →+ AdicCompletion (I.obj m) (M.obj m) :=
    { toFun z := Mhat.iso m (completedComponent Khat Mhat m g
        (Khat.obj.map f ((Khat.iso n).symm z)))
      map_zero' := by simp
      map_add' a b := by simp }
  let r : AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (K.obj n) →+ AdicCompletion (I.obj m) (M.obj m) :=
    { toFun z := Mhat.iso m (Mhat.obj.map f (completedComponent Khat Mhat n g'
        ((Khat.iso n).symm z)))
      map_zero' := by simp
      map_add' a b := by simp }
  have hl : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous (I.obj n) (I.obj m) l := by
    simpa [l, completedComponent, Function.comp_def] using
      (Khat.map_adicContinuous f).comp (I.obj n) (I.obj m) (I.obj m)
        (adicContinuous_adicCompletionMap (I.obj m) g)
  have hr : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous (I.obj n) (I.obj m) r := by
    simpa [r, completedComponent, Function.comp_def] using
      (adicContinuous_adicCompletionMap (I.obj n) g').comp
        (I.obj n) (I.obj n) (I.obj m) (Mhat.map_adicContinuous f)
  have hlr : l = r := adicContinuous_ext (I.obj n) (I.obj m) l r hl hr fun z => by
    change Mhat.iso m (completedComponent Khat Mhat m g
      (Khat.obj.map f ((Khat.iso n).symm (AdicCompletion.of (I.obj n) (K.obj n) z)))) =
      Mhat.iso m (Mhat.obj.map f (completedComponent Khat Mhat n g'
        ((Khat.iso n).symm (AdicCompletion.of (I.obj n) (K.obj n) z))))
    dsimp [completedComponent]
    rw [Khat.of_naturality]
    simp only [LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply, AdicCompletion.map_of]
    rw [Mhat.of_naturality, h]
  simpa [l, r] using congrArg (fun q => q (Khat.iso n x)) hlr

/-- The homomorphism of completions induced by a homomorphism of cosimplicial modules. -/
private noncomputable def completedHom
    {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}} (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A} (φ : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Hom K M)
    (Khat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I K)
    (Mhat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I M) :
    SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion.Hom Khat Mhat where
  hom :=
    { app n := AddCommGrpCat.ofHom (completedComponent Khat Mhat n (φ.app n))
      naturality := by
        intro n m f
        ext x
        exact completedComponent_naturality Khat Mhat f (φ.app m) (φ.app n)
          (fun z => (φ.naturality f z).symm) x }
  linear n r x := by
    apply (Mhat.iso n).injective
    simp [completedComponent]

/-- The `A_n`-linear component of a homotopy at a simplex `α` of `Δ[1]` in degree `n`. -/
private noncomputable def homotopyLinearMap
    {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}} {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A}
    {φ ψ : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Hom K M} (h : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Homotopy φ ψ)
    (n : SimplexCategory) (α : (Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).obj (op n)) :
    K.obj n →ₗ[A.obj n] M.obj n where
  toFun x := (h.homotopy.h.app n ≫ Pi.π _ α) x
  map_add' _x _y := map_add _ _ _
  map_smul' r x := h.linear n α r x

/-- The homotopy between the induced homomorphisms of completions obtained by completing
each component of a homotopy `h`. -/
private noncomputable def completedHomotopy
    {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}} (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A} {φ ψ : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Hom K M}
    (h : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Homotopy φ ψ)
    (Khat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I K)
    (Mhat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I M) :
    SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion.Homotopy
      (completedHom I φ Khat Mhat) (completedHom I ψ Khat Mhat) := by
  let c (n : SimplexCategory) (α : (Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).obj (op n)) :=
    AddCommGrpCat.ofHom (completedComponent Khat Mhat n (homotopyLinearMap h n α))
  have hex : ∃ H : Khat.obj ⟶ Mhat.obj.power Δ[1], ∀ n, H.app n = Pi.lift (c n) :=
    (CosimplicialObject.exists_hom_power_iff c).mpr (by
        intro n m f α
        ext x
        let orig (n : SimplexCategory) (α : (Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).obj (op n)) :
            K.toCosimplicialObject.obj n ⟶ M.toCosimplicialObject.obj n :=
          AddCommGrpCat.ofHom (homotopyLinearMap h n α).toAddHom
        have hnat := (CosimplicialObject.exists_hom_power_iff
          (U := K.toCosimplicialObject) (V := M.toCosimplicialObject) (K := Δ[1])
          orig).mp
            ⟨h.homotopy.h, fun n =>
              Pi.hom_ext _ _ fun α => (Pi.lift_comp_π (orig n) α).symm⟩ f α
        exact completedComponent_naturality Khat Mhat f (homotopyLinearMap h m α)
          (homotopyLinearMap h n ((Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).map f.op α))
          (fun z => congrArg (fun q => q z) hnat) x)
  have hH := Classical.choose_spec hex
  have hh (i : Fin 2) (χ : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Hom K M)
      (hχ : ∀ n z, homotopyLinearMap h n (SSet.stdSimplex.const 1 i (op n)) z = χ.app n z)
      (n : SimplexCategory) :
      (Classical.choose hex).app n ≫ Pi.π _ (SSet.stdSimplex.const 1 i (op n)) =
        (completedHom I χ Khat Mhat).hom.app n := by
    have hc := (hH n) ▸ (Pi.lift_comp_π (c n) (SSet.stdSimplex.const 1 i (op n)))
    refine hc.trans ?_
    ext x
    apply (Mhat.iso n).injective
    dsimp [c, completedHom, completedComponent]
    simp only [LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
    rw [LinearMap.ext (hχ n)]
  refine
    { homotopy :=
        { h := Classical.choose hex
          h₀ := hh 0 φ fun n z => congrArg (fun q => q z) (h.homotopy.h₀ n)
          h₁ := hh 1 ψ fun n z => congrArg (fun q => q z) (h.homotopy.h₁ n) }
      linear := fun n α r x => ?_ }
  apply (Mhat.iso n).injective
  have hc := (hH n) ▸ (Pi.lift_comp_π (c n) α)
  change Mhat.iso n
    (((Classical.choose hex).app n ≫ Pi.π (fun _ => Mhat.obj.obj n) α) (r • x)) =
    Mhat.iso n (r • (((Classical.choose hex).app n ≫
      Pi.π (fun _ => Mhat.obj.obj n) α) x))
  calc
    _ = Mhat.iso n ((c n α) (r • x)) := congrArg (Mhat.iso n) (congrArg (fun q => q (r • x)) hc)
    _ = Mhat.iso n (r • ((c n α) x)) := by
      dsimp [c, completedComponent]
      simp
    _ = _ := congrArg (fun y => Mhat.iso n (r • y)) (congrArg (fun q => q x) hc).symm

/-- Two homomorphisms of completions are equal when their underlying morphisms are. -/
private lemma completionHom_ext
    {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}} {I : CosimplicialIdeal A}
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A}
    {Khat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I K}
    {Mhat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I M}
    {f g : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion.Hom Khat Mhat} (h : f.hom = g.hom) : f = g := by
  cases f
  cases g
  cases h
  rfl

/-- **Stacks 07KQ, completion.** Homotopic homomorphisms of modules over a cosimplicial ring
induce homotopic homomorphisms on their completions with respect to a cosimplicial ideal. -/
@[stacks 07KQ "completion"]
public lemma homotopic_adicCompletionMap
    {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}} (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    {K M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, v} A} (φ ψ : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Hom K M)
    (h : Relation.EqvGen (fun a b => Nonempty (SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Homotopy a b)) φ ψ)
    (Khat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I K)
    (Mhat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion I M)
    (φhat ψhat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion.Hom Khat Mhat)
    (hφ : ∀ n x, Mhat.iso n (φhat.hom.app n x) =
      AdicCompletion.map (I.obj n) (φ.app n) (Khat.iso n x))
    (hψ : ∀ n x, Mhat.iso n (ψhat.hom.app n x) =
      AdicCompletion.map (I.obj n) (ψ.app n) (Khat.iso n x)) :
    Relation.EqvGen (fun a b =>
      Nonempty (SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion.Homotopy a b)) φhat ψhat :=
  by
    have key (χ : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Hom K M)
        (χhat : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.Completion.Hom Khat Mhat)
        (hχ : ∀ n x, Mhat.iso n (χhat.hom.app n x) =
          AdicCompletion.map (I.obj n) (χ.app n) (Khat.iso n x)) :
        χhat = completedHom I χ Khat Mhat := completionHom_ext <| by
      ext n x
      apply (Mhat.iso n).injective
      simpa [completedHom, completedComponent] using hχ n x
    rw [key φ φhat hφ, key ψ ψhat hψ]
    exact Relation.EqvGen.map (fun f => completedHom I f Khat Mhat)
      (fun _ _ h => ⟨completedHomotopy I h.some Khat Mhat⟩) h

end Completion

